# Engineering standards (retailer FE)

- **Ask, don’t guess** — stop on ambiguous requirements, missing env, unclear deploy target, or conflicting acceptance criteria.
- **Surgical changes** — smallest diff; no drive-by refactors or unrelated files.
- **Phased delivery** — break tickets into ordered phases when more than one concern is involved. One isolated change at a time; after each step: unit tests, run them, mini-review, then proceed. Do not pile up a large multi-file change and only test/review at the end.
- **Readable code** — match existing patterns; clear names; no cleverness.
- **Unit tests with the change** — Vitest, colocated `*.test.tsx` (or `*.test.ts`) next to the code under test. Run focused tests with `npm test` / vitest for the touched area.
- **Full test suite before merge readiness / push / PR** — always run `npm test` (vitest) green before marking a phase done for merge, and before push/`review-before-push`. Fix failures before continuing.
- **Negative QA before “done”** — list/run failure cases (auth missing, empty states, invalid IDs, permission denied, network errors, race/double-submit). Prefer at least one negative/edge test on critical paths.
- **No silent deploy** — never update sibling `retailer_web_build` `main` unless the user explicitly asks to deploy (and only via approved PR — see `pr-workflow`).
- **PR-only protected branches** — never commit/merge directly on `main` / `master` / `deploy/dev`; wait for review; never merge without ≥1 approval.
- **Review before push** — before any `git push`, present a short review (what changed, risks, tests, negative cases); wait for explicit go-ahead unless the user already said push/deploy.
- **Secret leakage on commit** — before every `git commit`, scan staged files; never stage `.env`, `*.pem`, `*.key`, service-account JSON, Firebase/Oracle keys, or hardcoded tokens/passwords. If sensitive, stop, unstage, and warn.
